<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Texan Santa Fe Expedition</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1841">1841</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Texan Santa Fe Expedition was a commercial and military venture sent by President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirabeau-b-lamar">Mirabeau B. Lamar</a> of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> in 1841 to bring the Santa Fe trade and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a>, which Texas claimed, under Texan control. About 320 men crossed the plains, suffered from hunger and attacks, and surrendered to Mexican forces without a fight. The prisoners were marched to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> and held until 1842.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/texan-santa-fe-expedition.jpg" alt="Texan Santa Fe Expedition" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NPS-graphics · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1845_trailmap.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
